cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "precorrect - method: a deterministic detector for how LLMs handle contested claims"
abstract: >-
  A methodology repository. It documents the five-outcome taxonomy (affirm / deny / evade /
  disqualify / distort) used to classify how a generated text positions itself toward a contested
  claim, the split between a form verdict computed from grammatical and discourse slots with zero
  LLM calls and a separate source-grounded content verdict, the pre-registered blind evaluation
  protocol with hash-frozen predictions, the rules governing rule adoption and human arbitration,
  and the generative-AI provenance posture. It contains no executable code, no benchmark cells and
  no knowledge base; the figures it reports are declared results of a private research project and
  are not reproducible from this repository.
type: dataset
